atter groups the lines of each invocation by correlationId, translates error codes into prose, runs forge logs itself and counts titles appearing in clear, which must always be zero."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_variables_and_events_reference_doc", "label": "Reference doc on trigger variables and events (who defines each name)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three groups: Atlassian manifest schema, what Jira delivers inside the event, and what this project invented; a missing name from the first two groups is never a fix for src/."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_changelog_no_value_leak_verification", "label": "Verified: Jira changelog does not leak field values in the trace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zero occurrences of from, to, fromString or toString in the real trace; only the field name survives."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_manual_test_guide_restructure", "label": "Manual test guide restructured to lead with the flow (Paso 0 activation, acceptance mapping)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A multi-perspective review found the guide demonstrated that an installation succeeded rather than what the trigger does; the trigger test now comes first and installation is an appendix."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_integration_service_contract_review", "label": "Contract review: integration-service matches the outbound client, zero incompatibilities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same limits on key and fields.summary, same single-issue-per-request rule and same 'a 201 is not success by itself' semantics; new finding: its 201 echoes the full input payload back, so the client must not re-log it."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_integration_plan_executed_tick_17", "label": "Real execution TICK-17: three invocations reached integration-service (201, successIntegration true)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forge correlationId matched the service X-Request-Id on every invocation; sanitized evidence saved as forge-to-integration-service-2026-08-29.txt; repository reverted to at-rest, no-egress state and integration-service was not modified."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_connect_forge_trigger_change_archived", "label": "OpenSpec change connect-forge-trigger-to-integration-service archived (24 tasks done)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_reduced_trigger_field_delivery_gap_closed", "label": "Gap closed: Jira delivers a reduced field set to triggers (DTJF-2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ten planted markers (name, email, phone, IBAN, amount, description, attachment, filename, title words) never reached the trace because Jira does not send description, attachment or custom fields; the allowlist would also have blocked them (two barriers). Caveat: payload.include.propertyPaths can request more fields."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_allowlist_design_held_against_reality", "label": "Allowlist design held against a real payload", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Real payload carried creator, reporter, fixVersions, associatedUsers, atlassianId, permissions and contextToken that fixtures never contained; none reached the built message."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_findings_worth_carrying_forward", "label": "Findings worth carrying forward (0.3.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_finding_ticket_produced_three_invocations", "label": "Finding: one ticket produced three invocations (0.3.0 changelog)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_events_doc_three_jiraeventtypename_subtypes", "label": "Fix: events doc now lists three jiraEventTypeName subtypes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "issue_updated appears alongside issue_generic for the same declared event depending on the touched field; logic should not rest on the subtype."}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_main_orphan_branch_documented", "label": "Fix: main documented as orphan branch (no formatter, no npm run logs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "bkt-jira-triggers/CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "bkt_jira_triggers_changelog_npm_flag_swallowing_fix", "label": "Fix: npm run logs --compact ignored; use t